  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Tied through six. Then the bats woke up in the eighth.",
    "what_this_means": "They needed someone to finish what the pitching set up, and they had two someones. V\u00e1squez gave them five clean innings and the bullpen didn't blink. Hart, Rodriguez, and Estrada combining for four scoreless with the game still tight. That was enough to work with, but only enough. Houston scored twice early and the Padres spent four innings chasing before Tatis Jr. drove in three across the middle innings to flip it. The game was decided when Hays went deep in the eighth. Two runs, insurance, no drama. This is what happens when the pitcher holds his ground and the offense answers: the Padres don't need to lead early to win.",
